# Documentation updates (required with code)

When you add, change, or remove a **user**, **route**, **binding**, **secret**, **tool**, **panel**, or **Phase**, update docs in the **same change set** (before considering the task done). Do not leave docs for “later” unless the user explicitly says so.

## Work notes split

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `WORK_NOTES.md` | **Archive** — §1 ~ §10.16. Do **not** append new feature/Phase sections. |
| `WORK_NOTES_2.md` | **Active** — §11 onward. All new non-trivial work notes go here. |
| `MERGE_STRATEGY.md` | **Baseline overlay** — A copy / B junction / C infra checklist for ~2-week port. |

## Mandatory

- **`WORK_NOTES_2.md` is always required** for non-trivial work:
  - New section (`## 11.` …) or Phase subsection (purpose, **수정 및 추가 파일**, curl/verify steps, what was *not* done)
  - Follow the “기록 규칙” block at the top of `WORK_NOTES_2.md`
  - Record local verification results when you (or the user) confirmed OK
- **`MERGE_STRATEGY.md` when portability boundaries change** — same change set:
  - New/moved **A** product modules (add/remove rows in the copy table)
  - Thicker/thinner **B** junctions (index / ChatAgent / App / wrangler / registry)
  - **C** infra (bindings, secrets, cron, R2/KV/DO)
  - Completed portability Wave — update Wave table + changelog date
  - Do **not** paste full Phase narratives here; link `WORK_NOTES_2.md`
- **Routing tree:** when HTTP paths change, update **`WORK_NOTES.md` §6 only** (single source). In the matching `WORK_NOTES_2.md` section, note “§6 반영” in one line — do not duplicate the full tree into `_2`.

Skip only for pure typo/style edits with no behavior or API surface change.

## Update when relevant (same PR / same session)

| Change type | Also update |
|-------------|-------------|
| New/changed Worker route or DO | `ARCHITECTURE.md` (feature table + backend layers), `CLAUDE.md` (routing / file map / repo layout) |
| New tool / panel / State field | `CLAUDE.md` file map; `ARCHITECTURE.md` tools/panels if listed |
| New binding, secret, cron, R2/KV/Vectorize | `CLAUDE.md` config table; `.dev.vars.example` + `worker-env.d.ts` for secrets; **`MERGE_STRATEGY.md` C (+ B if wrangler)** |
| Portability / module split (A thicker, B thinner) | **`MERGE_STRATEGY.md` A/B tables** (+ Wave row); detail in `WORK_NOTES_2.md` |
| Human onboarding / deploy steps | `README.md` and/or `README.eng.md` only if setup steps actually changed |
| LLM-facing architecture only | Prefer `CLAUDE.md`; do not duplicate long prose into README |

## Style

- Match existing `WORK_NOTES.md` / `WORK_NOTES_2.md` voice (Korean bullets, Phase tables, curl blocks).
- Keep `CLAUDE.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` concise — maps and pointers, not essays.
- Do not invent features in docs that are not in code.
- Prefer editing existing sections over adding parallel “shadow” docs.
- Do not copy archived §1–§10 content into `WORK_NOTES_2.md`; link to `WORK_NOTES.md` when needed.

## Checklist before “done”

1. Code works (or user verified).
2. `WORK_NOTES_2.md` updated (and `WORK_NOTES.md` §6 if routes changed).
3. `MERGE_STRATEGY.md` updated if A/B/C or Wave status changed.
4. Touched surfaces reflected in `ARCHITECTURE.md` / `CLAUDE.md` when the table above says so.
5. Mention docs in the commit message `Docs:` section when committing.
